      "id": 1,
      "text": "Evansville was originally called Vineyard when the post office opened in 1829, but the name changed to Evansville in 1836 to honor Captain Lewis Evans.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
