      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s post office has been in operation since 1838, making it one of the oldest continuously operating post offices in Arkansas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evansville%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Evansville’s early growth was fueled by the Indian Removal Act of 1830, which turned former Cherokee lands into a frontier farming and trading corridor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/evansville_arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s climate is humid subtropical, with hot, humid summers and mild winters typical of the Ozark Plateau region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
